Longer project description:\
SportaMath Lab is an interactive educational app I built with Python and Streamlit to help students learn math through sports simulations. The app includes a Race Pacing Simulator and a Basketball Shot Probability Visualizer. Students can adjust variables, compare strategies, view graphs, run simulations, and explore concepts such as averages, rates, standard deviation, probability, expected value, randomness, and optimization.\
I built SportaMath Lab to make math feel more connected to real life. It uses sports simulations to teach concepts like pacing, probability, expected value, and optimization. One module lets students compare race pacing strategies, and another lets them test basketball shot decisions using expected points and simulations. My goal was to make abstract math more interactive and intuitive.\
